{"page":473,"blocks":[{"x":0.65179,"y":0.05257,"w":0.29972,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"8.1 Using Basic Integration Formulas 459"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.09345,"w":0.06858,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Therefore,"},{"x":0.54046,"y":0.11233,"w":0.37644,"h":0.03309,"fs":0.01353,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"ax - 3 + 6 3x + 2b dx = x2 2 - 3x + 2 ln 0 3x + 20 + C."},{"x":0.41904,"y":0.11307,"w":0.12055,"h":0.03597,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"3x2 - 7x 3x + 2 dx = L"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.16379,"w":0.59305,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Reducing an improper fraction by long division (Example 5) does not always lead to an expression we can integrate directly. We see what to do about that in Section 8.5."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.21645,"w":0.17855,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 6 Evaluate"},{"x":0.63014,"y":0.24225,"w":0.04793,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3x + 2"},{"x":0.62431,"y":0.25011,"w":0.08485,"h":0.02366,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"21 - x2 dx."},{"x":0.3626,"y":0.27997,"w":0.31526,"h":0.01365,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution We first separate the integrand to get"},{"x":0.51636,"y":0.30492,"w":0.04793,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3x + 2"},{"x":0.6594,"y":0.30558,"w":0.02632,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x dx"},{"x":0.77802,"y":0.30558,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"},{"x":0.51053,"y":0.31211,"w":0.12882,"h":0.02432,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2 dx = 3 L"},{"x":0.64276,"y":0.31211,"w":0.10977,"h":0.02432,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2 + 2 L"},{"x":0.75594,"y":0.3128,"w":0.06701,"h":0.02364,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.34349,"w":0.30843,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"In the first of these new integrals, we substitute"},{"x":0.46695,"y":0.36843,"w":0.35509,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"u = 1 - x2, du = -2x dx, so x dx = -1"},{"x":0.81387,"y":0.37545,"w":0.03327,"h":0.02001,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2 du."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.40616,"w":0.10177,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Then we obtain"},{"x":0.61521,"y":0.41738,"w":0.06782,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(-1>2) du"},{"x":0.7209,"y":0.42961,"w":0.07963,"h":0.03214,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2L u-1>2 du"},{"x":0.52011,"y":0.43091,"w":0.02675,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x dx"},{"x":0.6381,"y":0.43093,"w":0.09098,"h":0.03082,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2u = - 3"},{"x":0.50367,"y":0.43745,"w":0.10977,"h":0.02432,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2 = 3 L"},{"x":0.60275,"y":0.45822,"w":0.04373,"h":0.03631,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2 # u1>2"},{"x":0.57232,"y":0.46674,"w":0.03861,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= - 3"},{"x":0.62199,"y":0.46878,"w":0.2168,"h":0.02614,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"1>2 + C1 = -321 - x2 + C1."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.50463,"w":0.33373,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The second of the new integrals is a standard form,"},{"x":0.53222,"y":0.52939,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"},{"x":0.51014,"y":0.53211,"w":0.3327,"h":0.02813,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2 = 2 sin-1 x + C2. Table 8.1, Formula 18"},{"x":0.4826,"y":0.5366,"w":0.02413,"h":0.02362,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 L"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.56662,"w":0.38456,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Combining these results and renaming C1 + C2 as C gives"},{"x":0.51818,"y":0.59139,"w":0.04793,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3x + 2"},{"x":0.51235,"y":0.59411,"w":0.30878,"h":0.0288,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"21 - x2 dx = -321 - x2 + 2 sin-1 x + C."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.64531,"w":0.5931,"h":0.05883,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"The question of what to substitute for in an integrand is not always quite so clear. Sometimes we simply proceed by trial-and-error, and if nothing works out, we then try another method altogether. The next several sections of the text present some of these new methods, but substitution works in the next example."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.72801,"w":0.17855,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 7 Evaluate"},{"x":0.62376,"y":0.75447,"w":0.08432,"h":0.03086,"fs":0.01441,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dx 11 + 2x23."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.80304,"w":0.59302,"h":0.04434,"fs":0.01441,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Solution We might try substituting for the term 2x, but we quickly realize the deriva- tive factor 1> 2x is missing from the integrand, so this substitution will not help. The other possibility is to substitute for 11 + 2x2, and it turns out this works:"},{"x":0.71211,"y":0.85082,"w":0.16024,"h":0.02547,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"u = 1 + 2x, du = 1 22x dx;"},{"x":0.58574,"y":0.85656,"w":0.08018,"h":0.03159,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2(u - 1) du u3"},{"x":0.46506,"y":0.85935,"w":0.11891,"h":0.03086,"fs":0.01441,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"dx 11 + 2x23 = L"},{"x":0.71211,"y":0.88199,"w":0.16024,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx = 22x du = 2(u - 1) du"},{"x":0.5873,"y":0.8996,"w":0.01976,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"a 2"},{"x":0.63417,"y":0.8996,"w":0.04442,"h":0.03203,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"u3b du"},{"x":0.59626,"y":0.90301,"w":0.04869,"h":0.0287,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u2 - 2"}]}